cff-version: 1.2.0
title: interactor-persona-frontier
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: K. S. Ernest (iFire)
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7772-8085
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-persona-frontier
abstract: >-
  The persona as an A2A webserver that learns its planning domain from
  experience. The planner (interactor-taskweft-persona, RECTGTN) is the fixed
  meta-method; the domain's content, which pipeline stage requires which and
  how long each takes, is induced from experience reports and frontier
  practice and lands only through a gate with a positive and a negative
  control. The domain is the look-dev pipeline for characters, props and
  worlds, all GPU-skinned, in their own stage subsets.
